 "supervisor_summary": "The five revised forecasts are nearly identical: median ~$96-97, sigma ~0.45, P(>= $94) ~0.52, P(< $66) ~20%, P(> $165) ~10%. My checks confirm their inputs. FY27 guidance was reaffirmed Sep 9, the September fade was macro (Brent ~$104, 10-year 5.1%), and FY27 FCF is only ~$0.7-0.8B because capex is guided at ~4% of sales. I trim the center by about a point (P(>= $94) 0.51), since the known oil/rates shock is already in the price, and set fair value at $96. Thesis break is $66. Confidence is low, so the forecasters' mean should stand.",
 "key_drivers": [
  "FY27 guide reaffirmed Sep 9: 3-5% organic growth, 12.7-13.5% adjusted operating margin, $3.10-3.35 EPS (33-34% tax, 368M shares). The full restructuring benefit lands in FY28, and mid-to-high-teens margins are 'over time' with no dated target. FY28 consensus EPS is ~$3.83, and the stock trades at ~25x.",
  "Macro: the US-Iran war keeps Brent near $104-108 (up ~20% in a month), and the 10-year Treasury yield hit 5.13% on Sep 23. That pressures multiples, US prestige spend and Middle East travel retail. A phased Hormuz deal under negotiation is the upside path.",
  "Cash: FY27 operating cash flow is guided at $1.3-1.4B with capex at ~4% of sales, so FCF is ~$0.7-0.8B, below the ~$0.5B dividend plus the $500M March-2027 maturity. Net debt is ~$3.8B.",
  "Realized vol is ~51-53% on 1-year and 2-year windows, with 20%+ gaps around earnings. The FY28 guide (Aug 2027) lands weeks before the horizon.",
  "Travel retail was reset to ~15% of sales, and Hainan is growing double digits. China was +9% organic, but North America is not yet gaining share after the Sep 1 sales-force reorganization."
 ],
